(vector (map (:db/id -1), (:adr/id 2799008350), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/date "2026-07-17"), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8350 — Ships' Deck Crews and Related Workers Deck-Crew Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8350)), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000 2607152500)), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2790003313-cloud-itonami-isco-3313-accounting-associate-professionals-coverage" "adr-2799005411-cloud-itonami-isco-5411-firefighters-coverage" "adr-2799005413-cloud-itonami-isco-5413-prison-guards-coverage")), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8350), (:actor/isco-08 "8350"), (:actor/name "Deck Crew Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:actor/domain :maritime/deck-crew-scheduling), (:actor/governor "DeckCrewGovernor"), (:actor/wave 2), (:actor/robotics? true), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-service-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :crew-member-provenance :effect-propose :vessel-provenance :crew-vessel-basis :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "initiate the mooring operation" "commence the mooring operation" "finalize the mooring operation" "finalize the mooring decision" "initiate the cargo-handling operation" "commence the cargo-handling operation" "finalize the cargo-handling operation" "finalize the cargo-handling decision" "commence deck work in heavy weather" "authorize deck work in heavy weather" "proceed with deck work in heavy weather" "override the deck officer's safety judgment" "override the deck officer")), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:actor/confidence-floor 0.6), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-service-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-service-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-service-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :flag-safety-concern}, :auto #{:log-service-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}}}"), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8350"), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8350"), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:test/simulator :deckcrew.actor-test), (:test/counts "{:total 20, :assertions 45, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :crew-member-verification :vessel-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-order-cost-threshold-escalation :safety-concern-always-escalates)), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799008350: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8350 Ships' Deck Crews and Related Workers deck-crew scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8350\n-- Ships' Deck Crews and Related Workers** only.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8350\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone (with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path) before\nany work began: `clojure -M -e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println\n(kotoba.occupation/get-occupation \\\"8350\\\"))\"` returned `{:id 8350,\n:name Ships' Deck Crews and Related Workers, :maturity :spec,\n:required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger],\n:optional-technologies [], :operating-states [:intake :propose\n:approve :execute :audit]}` -- the `:name` reads exactly \"Ships' Deck\nCrews and Related Workers\" (registry uses a curly apostrophe, U+2019,\nnot a straight quote), confirming the premise with no mismatch. Prior\nto this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`. This ADR and its companion registry edit\npromote the `8350` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nThis is a retry of a prior session that was cut off mid-task by a\nsession rate limit: the GitHub repository\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8350` had already been created (`gh\nrepo create` boilerplate only -- `.gitignore`/`CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`/\n`CONTRIBUTING.md`/`GOVERNANCE.md`/`LICENSE` -- confirmed empty of actor\nsource at task start) but no actor code had been pushed. On resuming\nthis task and re-cloning the target repository to confirm that empty\nstate, a concurrent sibling session in the same retry batch was found\nto have already completed and pushed a full, correct implementation to\n`main` (commit `82b4910faaa9238e92444254511acc27833d55ad`, same day).\nThis ADR's role is therefore to independently re-verify that\nconcurrent work end-to-end (full source read, fresh-clone test run,\nlint) rather than duplicate it, and to complete the remaining steps\n(this ADR, the registry promotion) that the concurrent session had not\nyet performed.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE by the\nconcurrent implementation, independently re-cloned and re-read in full\nduring this verification, is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313)\n(Accounting Associate Professionals: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/\n`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set).\n\n**Maritime deck-crew safety dimension.** Ships' Deck Crews perform\non-deck vessel operations (mooring, cargo securing, general\nseamanship) with real physical-safety stakes: fall overboard,\nentanglement in mooring lines, cargo-handling injury. This actor\ncoordinates CREW SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS ONLY -- it never performs a deck\noperation itself. The closed op allowlist and an independent\ncontent-based scope-exclusion check make it structurally impossible\nfor this actor's op-allowlist to ever include an op that directly\nfinalizes a mooring/cargo-handling operational decision, a\ndeck-work-in-heavy-weather go/no-go decision, or an override of a deck\nofficer's safety judgment -- these are always a hard, permanent block\nor an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible. This mirrors the\nguardrail shape established by **ADR-2607152500** (Wave4 rollout start\namendment): decisions directly touching a person's physical safety\nmust always exclude the closed op allowlist and always escalate to a\nhuman, not merely be gated behind a confidence threshold -- the same\nshape this fleet's ISCO-5411 (Firefighters), ISCO-5412 (Police\nOfficers) and ISCO-5413 (Prison Guards) actors applied to their own\nhigh-stakes domains.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8350` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for ships' deck crews,\nfollowing the SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Deck Crew Advisor ⊣\nDeckCrewGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- this is a different library coordinate from\nthe `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family),\nwith an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **crew-scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct deck-operation authority** -- it must NEVER be\ndesigned to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising ANY\nof: finalizing a mooring operation, finalizing a cargo-handling\noperational decision, deciding a heavy-weather deck-work go/no-go, or\noverriding a deck officer's safety judgment. These are not merely\ngated behind escalation for the op-selection dimension -- the closed\nfour-op allowlist structurally never contains such an op -- and, as\ndefense in depth against a compromised/malicious advisor, are also a\ncontent-based HARD block independent of which op was chosen.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-service-record` -- deck-work/watch-log data logging (routine\n  service-record entries; not a decision of any kind).\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- deck-crew watch/duty scheduling\n  proposal (a scheduling calendar action, never a mooring/cargo/\n  heavy-weather operational plan).\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface an equipment-defect/\n  weather-hazard/crew-fatigue concern; ALWAYS escalates to a human,\n  NEVER auto-commit-eligible.\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- deck-equipment (mooring lines, safety\n  gear) procurement proposal, gated by a cost-threshold escalation.\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nresembles directly finalizing a mooring/cargo-handling operational\ndecision, deciding a heavy-weather deck-work go/no-go, or overriding a\ndeck officer's safety judgment -- these are structurally absent from\nthe op-allowlist entirely, not merely gated behind escalation: the\nmock advisor's `infer` function only ever emits one of the four\nallowlist ops (driven by a `case` expression with no default branch\nproducing any other op shape), and if any code path (a forged\nproposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever produced such\nan op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check (`:op-not-allowed`)\nrejects it unconditionally and permanently -- verified by a dedicated\ntest (`hard-on-op-not-in-allowlist`) using a concretely-named forbidden\nop (`:finalize-mooring-operation`).\n\n### Six HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Crew-member provenance** -- the crew member must resolve to an\n   independently registered record (`:no-crew-member`). Never trusts\n   the proposal's own claim of who the crew member is.\n2. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`) -- the governor never dispatches hardware\n   and never performs a deck operation itself.\n3. **Vessel provenance** -- the vessel named in the proposal must\n   resolve to an independently registered record (`:no-vessel`).\n4. **Crew/vessel basis** -- the crew member's registered vessel\n   assignment must match the vessel named in the proposal\n   (`:crew-wrong-vessel`).\n5. **Closed op-allowlist** -- `:op` must be one of\n   `#{:log-service-record :schedule-crew-operation\n   :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order}`; any other op is a\n   HARD, PERMANENT block (`:op-not-allowed`) -- this is the structural\n   guarantee that no proposal can directly finalize a\n   mooring/cargo-handling operational decision or a heavy-weather\n   deck-work go/no-go decision through the op itself.\n6. **Scope exclusion** -- independent of the op-allowlist check, any\n   proposal whose free text (`:rationale`/`:detail`/`:action`) names a\n   finalization/execution action for a mooring operation, a\n   cargo-handling operation, commencing/authorizing deck work in heavy\n   weather, or overriding a deck officer's safety judgment is a HARD,\n   PERMANENT block (`:scope-exclusion`), evaluated unconditionally on\n   content. This is defense-in-depth against a compromised/malicious\n   advisor: even within an allowed op, free text cannot smuggle a\n   finalization decision through a `:rationale` or `:detail` field.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's `always-escalate-ops`). This is the ONLY\n  channel by which the robot may surface an equipment-defect/\n  weather-hazard/crew-fatigue observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the concern\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about it.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-order-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-at-exact-cost-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence.\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"mooring\", \"weather\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this domain's ordinary\nvocabulary legitimately mentions \"mooring\" (ordering mooring lines)\nand \"weather\" (flagging a weather hazard) in routine, in-scope\nproposals, making this bug class a live risk here specifically.\n`deckcrew.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTION phrases (e.g. \"initiate the mooring\noperation\", \"commence deck work in heavy weather\", \"override the\ndeck officer's safety judgment\"), never bare nouns, and\n`deckcrew.governor-test/never-self-trips-on-default-mock-advisor-proposals`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor across five\nrepresentative default requests (including a `:flag-safety-concern`\nfor a weather hazard, one for a mooring-winch equipment defect, and a\n`:coordinate-supply-order` for `[\"mooring lines\" \"fenders\"]`), never\ntrips `:scope-exclusion`. Confirmed green.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8350\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8350` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8350`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately before\n  the edit to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  retry batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`), independently re-run from a\n  fresh clone of the pushed repository during this verification pass:\n  20 tests, 45 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- Ad hoc `clj-kondo` lint of `src`/`test` (this actor's `deps.edn` does\n  not define a `:lint` alias, matching the verified\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` reference's own drift, independently\n  re-confirmed during this verification pass): 1 pre-existing\n  `Unresolved symbol: read-string` error in `deckcrew.advisor`'s\n  `llm-advisor` (the alternate real-LLM advisor swap point, not\n  exercised by the mock-advisor test suite) plus 2 unused-binding/\n  unused-referred-var warnings -- byte-for-byte the same lint\n  signature clj-kondo reports against the reference\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` repository itself, so this is a pre-existing\n  clj-kondo `.cljc` cross-platform quirk inherited from the mirrored\n  reference, not a regression introduced by this actor.\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-mooring-operation` or\n  `:approve-heavy-weather-deck-work` that is merely gated behind\n  `always-escalate-ops` (the shape `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for\n  `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`): rejected outright per the task's\n  explicit guidance and the `ADR-2607152500` precedent -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  mooring/cargo-handling decision or a heavy-weather go/no-go exists in\n  the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision\n  this severe against real physical-safety stakes (fall overboard,\n  entanglement, cargo-handling injury), the capability itself must not\n  exist. The only op related to safety escalation is\n  `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for human attention\n  and never itself decides, authorizes, or defers a deck operation for\n  later automatic execution.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"mooring\" \"weather\"\n  \"cargo\"]`): rejected outright per the task's explicit worked example\n  of this fleet's known self-tripping bug pattern -- this domain's own\n  vocabulary necessarily discusses mooring lines and weather hazards to\n  do its logistics/safety-flagging job, so a bare-noun list would risk\n  self-blocking the actor's own legitimate proposals (confirmed live by\n  the dedicated `never-self-trips-on-default-mock-advisor-proposals`\n  regression test).\n- Merging `crew-member` and `vessel` into a single entity (only\n  checking one provenance record): rejected -- the crew-wrong-vessel\n  check requires two independently registered entities so that a\n  vessel a crew member is not assigned to is caught even if both\n  records individually pass verification.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-service-record`** -- deck-work/watch-log data logging only\n   (crew id, vessel id, entry text). Not a decision of any kind, and\n   subject to the same scope-exclusion free-text check as every other\n   op.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- watch/duty scheduling logistics\n   only. Cannot carry a mooring/cargo-handling/heavy-weather\n   operational plan without tripping the scope-exclusion check if its\n   free text names a finalization/execution action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces an equipment-defect/\n   weather-hazard/crew-fatigue concern to a human; ALWAYS escalates\n   (governor's `always-escalate-ops`, unconditionally, at every\n   confidence level), NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY\n   channel through which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it\n   explicitly never resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself --\n   the human deck officer reviews and acts entirely on their own\n   authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- deck-equipment (mooring lines,\n   safety gear) procurement proposal, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates) like any office/facility\n   procurement workflow. Not an operational decision of any kind --\n   it is a purchasing-logistics action.\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nresembles directly finalizing a mooring/cargo-handling operational\ndecision, deciding a heavy-weather deck-work go/no-go, or overriding a\ndeck officer's safety judgment -- these are structurally absent,\nconfirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`deckcrew.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) a concretely-named forbidden-op\nfixture rejected at the governor-unit level\n(`deckcrew.governor-test/hard-on-op-not-in-allowlist`), and (c) a\ncontent-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op` field\n(`deckcrew.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases`,\n`deckcrew.governor/scope-violation?`), tested directly against\nmooring-finalization, heavy-weather-go/no-go and\ndeck-officer-override phrasings\n(`deckcrew.governor-test/hard-on-scope-exclusion-mooring-finalization-phrase`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-exclusion-heavy-weather-go-no-go-phrase`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-exclusion-officer-override-phrase`).\n")))
